{
  "name": "form-controls",
  "description": "Column holding the nine form controls and extra buttons with every prop each can carry on the wire, each bound as the demo binds it (value a pageState Value, onChange a SetState of the same key to the event's `value`): a tristate Checkbox on `agree` (true) with a label and all four colours, and a second Checkbox, true, labelled and enabled false; two Radios on one group `pick` (\"a\") with values \"a\" and \"b\", colours, the second enabled; a Switch on `notify` (true) with all four colours; a Slider on `level` (50) with min 0, max 100, divisions 4, trackHeight 6, a label and three colours; a Form around a TextFormField on `name` (\"Ada\") with placeholder, inputType, obscureText false, maxLines 1, maxLength 40, a style and a validator; an IconButton around an Icon with colour, size 32, tooltip, splash and highlight colours, padding 4, alignment topLeft and constraints; a mini FloatingActionButton around an Icon with background, elevation 6, tooltip, three colours, heroTag and isExtended false; and an InkWell around a Text with borderRadius 12 and splash and highlight colours (#RRGGBBAA). The buttons and the InkWell store which trigger fired in `lastTap` (onTap and onLongPress; the InkWell also onDoubleTap). Every static prop reaches the wire unchanged, every binding stays a state Value with its key in the node's watches, every action rides on its node, and every client resolver resolves each prop to the listed value. No node sends `stateKey`: no engine class declares it.",
